      "title": "Research: Rapid Charging Fund pilot: process evaluation",
      "summary": "Research and analysis Rapid Charging Fund pilot: process evaluation Evaluation of a pilot scheme aimed at funding electricity upgrades at motorway services to support ultra-rapid EV charging and inform future policy. From: Department for Transport Published: 8 September 2026 Get emails about this page Applies to England Documents Rapid charging fund pilot: process evaluation report PDF , 477 KB , 32 pages This file may not be suitable for users of assistive technology. Request an accessible format. If you use assistive technology (such as a screen reader) and need a version of this document in a more accessible format, please email webmasterdft@dft.gov.uk . Please tell us what format you need. It will help us if you say what assistive technology you use. Details The Rapid Charging Fund ( RCF ) was announced in 2020 to improve electric vehicle ( EV ) charging on the strategic road network ( SRN ). The RCF pilot was launched in 2023 to test using capital grants to support delivery of electricity network upgrades at motorway service areas, where high costs are a barrier to improvements in EV charging provision. This report, from Frontier Economics, is an independent process evaluation of the pilot, it assesses the effectiveness of the approach and identifies lessons for future policy design and implementation. Updates to this page Published 8 September 2026 Sign up for emails or print this page Get emails about this page Print this page",
